traces:\n   374→      - prd001-testutils R1.1\n   375→\n   376→  - name: rundifftests_matching_output\n   377→    description: RunDiffTests passes silently when both binaries produce identical output.\n   378→    inputs:\n   379→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n   380→      setup: \"both mock binaries print \\\"hello\\\\n\\\" to stdout and exit 0\"\n   381→    expected:\n   382→      postcondition: test passes with no output to stdout or stderr\n   383→    traces:\n   384→      - prd001-testutils R2.1\n   385→      - prd001-testutils R2.4\n   386→      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n   387→\n   388→  - name: rundifftests_divergent_stdout\n   389→    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when stdout differs between binaries.\n   390→    inputs:\n   391→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n   392→      setup: \"Go binary prints \\\"hello\\\\n\\\", reference prints \\\"world\\\\n\\\"\"\n   393→    expected:\n   394→      postcondition: \"test fails with message containing args, stdin, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes\"\n   395→    traces:\n   396→      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n   397→      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n   398→\n   399→  - name: rundifftests_divergent_exit_code\n   400→    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when exit codes differ.\n   401→    inputs:\n   402→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n   403→      setup: \"Go binary exits 0, reference exits 1\"\n   404→    expected:\n   405→      postcondition: test fails with message showing both exit codes\n   406→    traces:\n   407→      - prd001-testutils R3.4\n   408→      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n   409→\n   410→  - name: timestamp_normalizer\n   411→    description: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so time-dependent outputs match.\n   412→    inputs:\n   413→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Normalize: []NormalizeFunc{TimestampNormalizer}\"\n   414→      setup: \"binaries produce outputs differing only in timestamp field\"\n   415→    expected:\n   416→      postcondition: test passes after normalization strips timestamps\n   417→    traces:\n   418→      - prd001-testutils R4.1\n   419→      - prd001-testutils R4.2\n   420→\n   421→  - name: compose_normalizers\n   422→    description: ComposeNormalizers chains multiple functions applied in order.\n   423→    inputs:\n   424→      function: \"testutils.ComposeNormalizers(fn1, fn2)\"\n   425→    expected:\n   426→      postcondition: \"composed function applies fn1 then fn2; output matches fn2(fn1(input))\"\n   427→    traces:\n   428→      - prd001-testutils R4.3\n   429→      - prd001-testutils R4.4\n   430→\n   431→  - name: expected_files_match\n   432→    description: ExpectedFiles comparison passes when Go binary writes correct file content.\n   433→    inputs:\n   434→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n   435→      setup: \"mock binary writes expected content to output file\"\n   436→    expected:\n   437→      postcondition: test passes with no output\n   438→    traces:\n   439→      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n   440→      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n   441→\n   442→  - name: expected_files_diverge\n   443→    description: ExpectedFiles comparison fails when Go binary writes wrong file content.\n   444→    inputs:\n   445→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n   446→      setup: \"mock binary writes different content than expected\"\n   447→    expected:\n   448→      postcondition: test fails with message showing file path, expected content, actual content\n   449→    traces:\n   450→      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n   451→      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n   452→\n   453→  - name: timeout_exceeded\n   454→    description: RunDiffTests fails with timeout message when binary exceeds timeout.\n   455→    inputs:\n   456→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with short timeout\"\n   457→      setup: \"mock binary sleeps beyond timeout\"\n   458→    expected:\n   459→      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n   460→    traces:\n   461→      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n   462→\n   463→  - name: env_default_lc_all\n   464→    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n   465→    inputs:\n   466→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n   467→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   468→    expected:\n   469→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n   470→    traces:\n   471→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   472→\n   473→  - name: env_override_lc_all\n   474→    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n   475→    inputs:\n   476→      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n   477→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   478→    expected:\n   479→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n   480→    traces:\n   481→      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n   482→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   483→\n   484→  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n   485→    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n   486→    inputs:\n   487→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n   488→      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n   489→    expected:\n   490→      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n   491→    traces:\n   492→      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n   493→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"689ac570-29e0-4413-baf9-70f9ba09ab2a","uuid":"7ad81ad2-5c79-40df-b4ac-e2f965893eae","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/129/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel00.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel00.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\nrelease: rel00.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n  - prd011-magefiles R1\n  - prd011-magefiles R2\n  - prd011-magefiles R3\n  - prd011-magefiles R4\n  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n  - prd003-format R1\n  - prd003-format R2\n  - prd003-format R3\n  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n  - prd002-sys R1\n  - prd002-sys R2\n  - prd002-sys R3\n  - prd002-sys R4\n  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n  - prd001-testutils R1\n  - prd001-testutils R2\n  - prd001-testutils R3\n  - prd001-testutils R4\n  - prd001-testutils R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n\ntest_cases:\n  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n\n  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n\n  - name: version_prints_tag\n    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n\n  - name: version_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 2\n      stdout: \"\"\n      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_dev_build\n    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    inputs:\n      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n\n  - name: lint_passes\n    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage lint\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n\n  - name: clean_removes_bin\n    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  - name: clean_idempotent\n    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n\n  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n    expected:\n      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n      - prd003-format R1.4\n\n  - name: columns_empty_input\n    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n    expected:\n      result: nil\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n\n  - name: pad_right\n    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: pad_left\n    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: display_width_multibyte\n    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.3\n\n  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n      regular: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.1\n      - prd003-format R2.4\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled\n    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.2\n\n  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n    expected:\n      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n      reset: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.6\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n    expected:\n      color_enabled_pipe: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.7\n\n  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: human_size_binary\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n      - prd003-format R3.3\n\n  - name: human_size_si\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n\n  - name: human_size_zero\n    description: HumanSize returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(0, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"0\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.4\n\n  # --- uc003-sys: pkg/sys syscall abstractions ---\n\n  - name: terminal_width_pipe\n    description: TerminalWidth returns an error when stdout is a pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.TerminalWidth() with stdout redirected to a pipe\"\n    expected:\n      error: non-nil\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.1\n\n  - name: is_terminal_pipe_fd\n    description: IsTerminal returns false for a pipe file descriptor.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.IsTerminal(pipeFd)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.3\n\n  - name: stat_known_file\n    description: Stat returns correct extended metadata for a known file.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks match stat(1) output\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: lstat_symlink\n    description: Lstat on a symlink returns symlink type bits, not target's mode.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Lstat(symlinkPath)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"Mode & os.ModeSymlink != 0\"\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n\n  - name: stat_modtime_populated\n    description: Stat returns a non-zero ModTime from the platform-correct field.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: ModTime is non-zero and close to os.Stat(testFile).ModTime()\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.3\n\n  - name: stat_hard_link_count\n    description: Stat returns correct Nlink for a file with multiple hard links.\n    inputs:\n      setup: \"create testFile, create hard link to testFile\"\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink == 2\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: sigpipe_handler_exit_zero\n    description: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() then write to closed pipe\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R3.1\n\n  - name: on_terminal_resize_callback\n    description: OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked on SIGWINCH.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.OnTerminalResize(callback) then send SIGWINCH\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: callback was called with a positive width\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R4.1\n      - prd002-sys R4.2\n\n  - name: cross_platform_compile\n    description: All pkg/sys code compiles on darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 go build ./pkg/sys/ && GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./pkg/sys/\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.2\n\n  # --- uc004-testutils: pkg/testutils differential testing harness ---\n\n  - name: difftest_zero_value\n    description: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, echoBin, echoBin, []DiffTest{{Name: \\\"zero\\\"}})\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.1\n\n  - name: rundifftests_matching_output\n    description: RunDiffTests passes silently when both binaries produce identical output.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"both mock binaries print \\\"hello\\\\n\\\" to stdout and exit 0\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output to stdout or stderr\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.1\n      - prd001-testutils R2.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_stdout\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when stdout differs between binaries.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary prints \\\"hello\\\\n\\\", reference prints \\\"world\\\\n\\\"\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"test fails with message containing args, stdin, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_exit_code\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when exit codes differ.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary exits 0, reference exits 1\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing both exit codes\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: timestamp_normalizer\n    description: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so time-dependent outputs match.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Normalize: []NormalizeFunc{TimestampNormalizer}\"\n      setup: \"binaries produce outputs differing only in timestamp field\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes after normalization strips timestamps\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.1\n      - prd001-testutils R4.2\n\n  - name: compose_normalizers\n    description: ComposeNormalizers chains multiple functions applied in order.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.ComposeNormalizers(fn1, fn2)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"composed function applies fn1 then fn2; output matches fn2(fn1(input))\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.3\n      - prd001-testutils R4.4\n\n  - name: expected_files_match\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison passes when Go binary writes correct file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes expected content to output file\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: expected_files_diverge\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison fails when Go binary writes wrong file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes different content than expected\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing file path, expected content, actual content\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: timeout_exceeded\n    description: RunDiffTests fails with timeout message when binary exceeds timeout.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with short timeout\"\n      setup: \"mock binary sleeps beyond timeout\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n\n  - name: env_default_lc_all\n    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: env_override_lc_all\n    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n","numLines":493,"startLine":1,"totalLines":493}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J5ksYQDdqj4HJQmn3gbhnY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n     2→title: \"Execute differential tests and compare binary outputs via pkg/testutils\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator verifies that pkg/testutils correctly executes Go and reference binaries\n     6→  with identical inputs, compares their outputs, and reports divergence. The test exercises\n     7→  each harness capability in isolation: RunDiffTests runs named subtests and compares\n     8→  stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte; normalization hooks strip non-deterministic\n     9→  fields before comparison; ComposeNormalizers chains multiple hooks; file-state comparison\n    10→  validates output files for utilities like sponge; and the timeout mechanism prevents\n    11→  hanging test runs.\n    12→\n    13→actor: Human Operator\n    14→\n    15→trigger: |\n    16→  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd001-testutils.yaml) and wants to verify\n    17→  that pkg/testutils satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n    18→\n    19→flow:\n    20→  - id: F1\n    21→    step: |\n    22→      The operator runs go test ./pkg/testutils/... which executes the unit tests for\n    23→      pkg/testutils. Unlike cmd/ packages that use differential testing against a reference\n    24→      binary, pkg/testutils is the harness itself. Its tests use mock binaries (small shell\n    25→      scripts or compiled test helpers) that produce known stdout, stderr, and exit codes.\n    26→  - id: F2\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The DiffTest struct test verifies that all fields are accessible and that the zero\n    29→      value produces a valid test case: no args, nil stdin (EOF), nil env (defaults with\n    30→      LC_ALL=C), empty WorkDir (t.TempDir), exit code 0, no normalization, no expected\n    31→      files.\n    32→  - id: F3\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      The RunDiffTests matching-output test creates two mock binaries that produce identical\n    35→      stdout and stderr, then calls RunDiffTests. The test passes silently with no output.\n    36→  - id: F4\n    37→    step: |\n    38→      The RunDiffTests divergent-output test creates two mock binaries that produce different\n    39→      stdout. RunDiffTests calls t.Fatal with a failure message containing the args, stdin,\n    40→      both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes.\n    41→  - id: F5\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The normalization test creates mock binaries whose outputs differ only in a timestamp\n    44→      field. TimestampNormalizer strips the timestamp before comparison, making the test pass.\n    45→  - id: F6\n    46→    step: |\n    47→      The ComposeNormalizers test chains two normalizer functions and verifies they are\n    48→      applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison.\n    49→  - id: F7\n    50→    step: |\n    51→      The file-state comparison test uses mock binaries that write to files in the working\n    52→      directory. DiffTest.ExpectedFiles specifies the expected content. The test verifies\n    53→      that matching content passes and divergent content fails with the correct report.\n    54→  - id: F8\n    55→    step: |\n    56→      The timeout test creates a mock binary that sleeps beyond the configured timeout.\n    57→      RunDiffTests fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging.\n    58→  - id: F9\n    59→    step: |\n    60→      The environment default test verifies that LC_ALL=C is set when DiffTest.Env is nil,\n    61→      and that an explicit Env entry overrides the default.\n    62→\n    63→touchpoints:\n    64→  - T1: \"pkg/testutils — DiffTest, NormalizeFunc (prd001-testutils R1)\"\n    65→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, WorkDir, LC_ALL default (prd001-testutils R2)\"\n    66→  - T3: \"pkg/testutils — comparison and divergence reporting (prd001-testutils R3)\"\n    67→  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers (prd001-testutils R4)\"\n    68→  - T5: \"pkg/testutils — ExpectedFiles file-state comparison (prd001-testutils R5)\"\n    69→\n    70→success_criteria:\n    71→  - id: S1\n    72→    criterion: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n    73→  - id: S2\n    74→    criterion: RunDiffTests produces no output when both binaries match.\n    75→  - id: S3\n    76→    criterion: RunDiffTests reports divergence with args, stdin, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    77→  - id: S4\n    78→    criterion: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so that time-dependent outputs match.\n    79→  - id: S5\n    80→    criterion: ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order and the composed result works as a single normalizer.\n    81→  - id: S6\n    82→    criterion: ExpectedFiles comparison passes for matching files and fails for divergent files.\n    83→  - id: S7\n    84→    criterion: Timeout produces a clear failure message rather than hanging.\n    85→  - id: S8\n    86→    criterion: LC_ALL=C is the default environment and DiffTest.Env overrides it.\n    87→  - id: S9\n    88→    criterion: go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures.\n    89→\n    90→out_of_scope:\n    91→  - Utility-specific normalizers (LsNormalizer, LsExtendedNormalizer) are defined in their\n    92→    respective cmd/ packages, not in pkg/testutils.\n    93→  - Binary compilation and installation are handled by magefiles, not pkg/testutils.\n    94→  - Retry logic and filesystem mocking are explicitly excluded by the PRD.\n    95→\n    96→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    97→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"689ac570-29e0-4413-baf9-70f9ba09ab2a","uuid":"bbde0433-e11b-45ff-8237-5978b5e10400","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/129/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc004-testutils\ntitle: \"Execute differential tests and compare binary outputs via pkg/testutils\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator verifies that pkg/testutils correctly executes Go and reference binaries\n  with identical inputs, compares their outputs, and reports divergence. The test exercises\n  each harness capability in isolation: RunDiffTests runs named subtests and compares\n  stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte; normalization hooks strip non-deterministic\n  fields before comparison; ComposeNormalizers chains multiple hooks; file-state comparison\n  validates output files for utilities like sponge; and the timeout mechanism prevents\n  hanging test runs.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd001-testutils.yaml) and wants to verify\n  that pkg/testutils satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs go test ./pkg/testutils/... which executes the unit tests for\n      pkg/testutils. Unlike cmd/ packages that use differential testing against a reference\n      binary, pkg/testutils is the harness itself. Its tests use mock binaries (small shell\n      scripts or compiled test helpers) that produce known stdout, stderr, and exit codes.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The DiffTest struct test verifies that all fields are accessible and that the zero\n      value produces a valid test case: no args, nil stdin (EOF), nil env (defaults with\n      LC_ALL=C), empty WorkDir (t.TempDir), exit code 0, no normalization, no expected\n      files.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The RunDiffTests matching-output test creates two mock binaries that produce identical\n      stdout and stderr, then calls RunDiffTests. The test passes silently with no output.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The RunDiffTests divergent-output test creates two mock binaries that produce different\n      stdout. RunDiffTests calls t.Fatal with a failure message containing the args, stdin,\n      both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The normalization test creates mock binaries whose outputs differ only in a timestamp\n      field. TimestampNormalizer strips the timestamp before comparison, making the test pass.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The ComposeNormalizers test chains two normalizer functions and verifies they are\n      applied in order to both stdout and stderr before comparison.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The file-state comparison test uses mock binaries that write to files in the working\n      directory. DiffTest.ExpectedFiles specifies the expected content. The test verifies\n      that matching content passes and divergent content fails with the correct report.\n  - id: F8\n    step: |\n      The timeout test creates a mock binary that sleeps beyond the configured timeout.\n      RunDiffTests fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging.\n  - id: F9\n    step: |\n      The environment default test verifies that LC_ALL=C is set when DiffTest.Env is nil,\n      and that an explicit Env entry overrides the default.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"pkg/testutils — DiffTest, NormalizeFunc (prd001-testutils R1)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, WorkDir, LC_ALL default (prd001-testutils R2)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/testutils — comparison and divergence reporting (prd001-testutils R3)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers (prd001-testutils R4)\"\n  - T5: \"pkg/testutils — ExpectedFiles file-state comparison (prd001-testutils R5)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: RunDiffTests produces no output when both binaries match.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: RunDiffTests reports divergence with args, stdin, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so that time-dependent outputs match.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order and the composed result works as a single normalizer.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: ExpectedFiles comparison passes for matching files and fails for divergent files.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: Timeout produces a clear failure message rather than hanging.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: LC_ALL=C is the default environment and DiffTest.Env overrides it.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Utility-specific normalizers (LsNormalizer, LsExtendedNormalizer) are defined in their\n    respective cmd/ packages, not in pkg/testutils.\n  - Binary compilation and installation are handled by magefiles, not pkg/testutils.\n  - Retry logic and filesystem mocking are explicitly excluded by the PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
